# Every text file is LF in the repository and in the working tree, whatever the clone's core.autocrlf says. Git for
# Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks text out with CRLF: bash under WSL then fails on the scripts
# ($'\r': command not found), and the generated .vsm / .mk / headers no longer match their generators
# (tools/ci/offline.sh). eol=lf keeps a Windows checkout byte-identical to a Linux one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The README images (docs/, tools/ci/hygiene.py allows only these): never converted or diffed as text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
